in @prism
in @meta
in @epistemologic

# @epistemologic/reality — the substrate's discipline for what physically exists.
#
# The recognition (2026-06-06, Reed + Alex → Mara): silicon, time, and the
# species that follow (space, matter, biology, social) are all members of
# a single family — the substrate's vocabulary for what is OBSERVER-RELATIVE
# and BOUNDED BY THE HARDWARE FLOOR. The family root names the discipline;
# the species declare their carriers under it.
#
# === Discipline ===
#
# Reality is what the observer can SEE under measurement, bounded by the
# local hardware's precision. The same speed-of-light analogue that
# @lens/transit makes operational at the measurement altitude:
#
#   - measurable: each carrier carries a detect() primitive that reads
#                 the running system; the result is content-addressed.
#   - bounded:    every measurement is bounded by a hardware floor named
#                 explicitly in the carrier's discipline; the substrate
#                 is honest about what it cannot observe.
#   - observable-or-explicitly-not: where the floor cannot reach (e.g.
#                 PMC access denied on locked-down platforms), the
#                 substrate states the absence STRUCTURALLY rather than
#                 pretending the value is missing.
#
# The discipline lifts from @epistemologic.literal (the name-IS-the-thing
# verifier): a reality carrier's identity IS its measurement; re-detection
# under the same conditions must content-address to the same OID. The
# literal property is the universal verdict surface for every reality
# species.
#
# === Species under this family ===
#
# Currently loaded:
#
#   @epistemologic/reality/silicon         the running CPU + memory.
#                                          arch (arm64/x86_64), memory model,
#                                          compute_bound, flake_ref. Migrated
#                                          from shards/epistemologic/silicon/
#                                          2026-06-06 (Mara).
#   @epistemologic/reality/time            the substrate's time discipline.
#                                          duration, monotonic, wall, instant,
#                                          tick. Lifted from boot/std/time.mirror
#                                          2026-06-06 (Mara).
#
# Future species — land when a consumer pulls (per Last Responsible Moment):
#
#   @epistemologic/reality/space           the substrate's spatial vocabulary.
#                                          Network topology, geographic locale,
#                                          shard placement.
#   @epistemologic/reality/matter          mass / energy / persistent storage.
#                                          Substrate-pull surface for the
#                                          disk / battery / thermal envelope.
#   @epistemologic/reality/biology         the human carrier. Heartbeat,
#                                          presence, embodiment signals when a
#                                          consumer pulls.
#   @epistemologic/reality/social          the multi-party carrier. Peers,
#                                          consent boundaries, conversation.
#
# === Why a family root ===
#
# Per [[architecture-prism-as-trait-as-everything]] every kind that stands
# on its own discipline is a prism. Reality IS such a kind: a substrate-
# wide vocabulary for what physically exists, with a shared verification
# discipline (literal-by-re-measurement), a shared honesty contract
# (hardware-floor declaration), and multiple species that each carry their
# own structural meaning under the same discipline.
#
# The previous shape (silicon and time as siblings at the epistemologic
# root, time inside boot/std/) under-declared the inheritance. Reality
# names the shared parent; species inherit through `in @epistemologic/reality`
# at the top of their files (cf. the @uuid root and @uuid/spectral sub-
# prism precedent, 2026-06-06 first tick).
#
# Spec context: docs/insights/2026-05-25-time-as-substrate-and-postgres-heritage.md
#               (time discipline), docs/specs/shard-design.md (silicon
#               carriers), fragmentation/docs/specs/lens-transit.md
#               (the hardware-floor analogue at the measurement altitude).
# Substrate decisions: [[architecture-shards-as-substrate-source]],
#                      [[architecture-prism-as-trait-as-everything]],
#                      [[architecture-lift-as-load-bearing]].
# Related shards: epistemologic/reality/silicon.mirror (the first species
#                 root), epistemologic/reality/time.mirror (the second
#                 species root).
# Path-namespace property: this file at `shards/epistemologic/reality.mirror`
# declares `@epistemologic/reality` and only that.

out @epistemologic/reality
